{%- comment -%}
  Collection (D03 / D04 desktop, M04 / M05 phone) — Nov 2026 layout, after
  the Aritzia collection page the owner picked as the reference:

  1. Top: a breadcrumb, the page's name with its product count, then the
     categories as a row of photo tiles (alp-cat-tiles) — View all, each
     product Type, coming-soon collections, the collections — the one
     you're on outlined.
  2. Tools: the most-used filters as buttons straight away (Size, Colour),
     then All filters; Sort by at the right from the Theme settings
     threshold up. This row pins under the header once scrolled to.
  3. Products straight after, on the first screen: bare cards, four across
     on desktop, two on phones. The first card plays the product's video
     when it has one (alp-card, video: true).
  4. The story (an Intro block, or a collection's image and description):
     an editorial card in the grid after the second row on desktop / the
     fourth on phones — the eighth product either way — or straight after
     the products while there are fewer. Page one only.

  Type headings only appear when a page mixes two or more Types and no
  filter or sort is on; the tiles do that job otherwise.

  Filters are Shopify's (Search & Discovery), so they exist on collection
  pages but not on Shopify's automatic Type pages. A collection named after
  a Type (handle "shorts" for Type "Shorts") takes that Type's place in the
  tiles and menus, which is how a Type gets filters. Desktop drops the
  filters under the tools row; on a phone the same form is a bottom sheet
  with accordions. "Show N results" is a live count — alpine.js re-asks
  this section for its count as the boxes change.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign threshold = settings.alp_filter_threshold | default: 6
  assign show_sort = false
  if collection.all_products_count >= threshold
    assign show_sort = true
  endif
  assign show_filters = false
  if collection.filters.size > 0
    assign show_filters = true
  endif
  assign show_tools = false
  if show_filters or show_sort
    assign show_tools = true
  endif

  assign active = 0
  for f in collection.filters
    assign active = active | plus: f.active_values.size
    if f.type == 'price_range'
      if f.min_value.value != blank or f.max_value.value != blank
        assign active = active | plus: 1
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign count = collection.products_count
  assign coming_soon = false
  if collection.all_products_count == 0 and collection.handle != 'all' and collection.current_type == blank
    assign coming_soon = true
  endif
  if coming_soon
    assign show_tools = false
    assign show_filters = false
  endif

  assign page_title = collection.title
  if collection.current_type != blank
    assign page_title = collection.current_type
  elsif collection.handle == 'all'
    assign page_title = 'All products'
  endif
  assign sort_by = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by

  assign codes = section.settings.codes | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
-%}

{%- paginate collection.products by 24 -%}
<section
  class="alp alp-cat"
  data-alp-cat
  data-alp-section="{{ section.id }}"
  data-alp-count="{{ count }}"
>
  {%- liquid
    comment
      The page's own story: a Type page looks up its Type, a collection its
      handle (so "Shorts" matches both the Type and a collection with the
      handle shorts); a collection without a block falls back to its image
      and description. The all-products page has none.
    endcomment
    assign page_key = ''
    if collection.current_type != blank
      assign page_key = collection.current_type | handleize
    elsif collection.handle != 'all'
      assign page_key = collection.handle | handleize
    endif
    assign page_block = nil
    if page_key != ''
      for b in section.blocks
        assign bk = b.settings.match | handleize
        if bk == page_key
          assign page_block = b
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The story is captured here and placed in the grid further down, so the
    products come first.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture story -%}
    {%- unless coming_soon -%}
      {%- if page_block != nil -%}
        {%- assign story_title = page_block.settings.title | default: page_title -%}
        {%- render 'alp-cat-intro', title: story_title, tagline: page_block.settings.tagline, text: page_block.settings.text, image: page_block.settings.image, attrs: page_block.shopify_attributes -%}
      {%- elsif collection.current_type == blank and collection.handle != 'all' and collection.image != blank -%}
        {%- assign story_text = collection.description | strip_html | strip -%}
        {%- render 'alp-cat-intro', title: collection.title, text: story_text, image: collection.image -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if paginate.current_page > 1 -%}{%- assign story = '' -%}{%- endif -%}

  <div class="alp-plp__top">
    {%- if coming_soon -%}
      {%- comment -%} Its Notify me page already carries the name. {%- endcomment -%}
      <h1 class="alp-vh">{{ page_title | escape }}</h1>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- unless collection.handle == 'all' and collection.current_type == blank -%}
        <p class="alp-plp__crumbs"><a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Shop</a> <span aria-hidden="true">—</span> <span>{{ page_title | escape }}</span></p>
      {%- endunless -%}
      <h1 class="alp-plp__title">{{ page_title | escape }} <sup aria-hidden="true">{{ count }}</sup><span class="alp-vh"> — {{ count }} {% if count == 1 %}product{% else %}products{% endif %}</span></h1>
    {%- endif -%}
    <nav class="alp-plp__tiles" aria-label="Categories">
      {%- render 'alp-cat-tiles', all_image: section.settings.all_image -%}
    </nav>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The tools row and the Filters panel stay pinned to the top once scrolled
    to; the header slides in above them on the way up (alpine.css,
    "alp-cat__head").
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="alp-cat__head">
  {%- if show_tools -%}
  <div class="alp-plp__tools">
    {%- if show_filters -%}
      {%- liquid
        comment
          The filters people reach for first, as buttons: Size and Colour
          where the collection has them, else its first two filters.
        endcomment
        assign quick = ''
        for f in collection.filters
          assign fl = f.label | downcase
          if fl contains 'size' or fl contains 'colour' or fl contains 'color'
            assign quick = quick | append: forloop.index0 | append: ','
          endif
        endfor
        if quick == ''
          for f in collection.filters limit: 2
            assign quick = quick | append: forloop.index0 | append: ','
          endfor
        endif
        assign quick = quick | split: ','
      -%}
      {%- for f in collection.filters -%}
        {%- assign idx = forloop.index0 | append: '' -%}
        {%- unless quick contains idx -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
        {%- assign on_n = f.active_values.size -%}
        <button class="alp-plp__chip{% if on_n > 0 %} is-on{% endif %}" type="button" data-alp-toggle="alp-filters" data-alp-filter-jump="{{ forloop.index0 }}" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="alp-filters">
          {{- f.label | replace: 'Color', 'Colour' | replace: 'color', 'colour' | escape }}{% if on_n > 0 %} ({{ on_n }}){% endif -%}
        </button>
      {%- endfor -%}
      <button class="alp-plp__chip{% if active > 0 %} is-on{% endif %}" type="button" data-alp-toggle="alp-filters" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="alp-filters">
        All filters{% if active > 0 %} ({{ active }}){% endif %}
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="alp-cat__spacer"></span>
    {%- if show_sort -%}
      <label class="alp-cat__sort alp-d">
        <span class="alp-vh">Sort by</span>
        <select name="sort_by" form="alp-filter-form" data-alp-autosubmit>
          {%- for o in collection.sort_options -%}
            <option value="{{ o.value | escape }}"{% if o.value == sort_by %} selected{% endif %}>{% if forloop.first %}Sort by: {% endif %}{{ o.name | escape }}</option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </select>
      </label>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if show_tools -%}
    <div class="alp-filters" id="alp-filters" data-alp-panel data-alp-sheet hidden>
      <form class="alp-filters__form" id="alp-filter-form" action="{{ collection.url }}" method="get" data-alp-filter-form>
        <div class="alp-sheet__grab alp-m" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="alp-sheet__head alp-m">
          <span>Filters</span>
          <button class="alp-x" type="button" data-alp-close aria-label="Close filters">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="alp-filters__groups">
          {%- for f in collection.filters -%}
            {%- assign is_size = false -%}
            {%- assign label_down = f.label | downcase -%}
            {%- if label_down contains 'size' -%}{%- assign is_size = true -%}{%- endif -%}
            <details class="alp-filters__group"{% if forloop.first or f.active_values.size > 0 %} open{% endif %}>
              <summary class="alp-filters__head">{{ f.label | replace: 'Color', 'Colour' | replace: 'color', 'colour' | escape }}<span class="alp-menu__pm alp-m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
              {%- case f.type -%}
                {%- when 'price_range' -%}
                  <div class="alp-filters__price">
                    <label><span>From</span>
                      <input type="number" name="{{ f.min_value.param_name }}" value="{{ f.min_value.value | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}" placeholder="0" min="0" inputmode="decimal">
                    </label>
                    <label><span>To</span>
                      <input type="number" name="{{ f.max_value.param_name }}" value="{{ f.max_value.value | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}" placeholder="{{ f.range_max | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}" min="0" inputmode="decimal">
                    </label>
                  </div>
                {%- else -%}
                  <div class="alp-filters__values{% if is_size %} alp-filters__values--sizes{% endif %}">
                    {%- for v in f.values -%}
                      {%- liquid
                        assign code = ''
                        for line in codes
                          assign pair = line | strip | split: ':'
                          if pair.size == 2
                            assign k = pair[0] | strip | downcase
                            assign vl = v.label | downcase
                            if k == vl
                              assign code = pair[1] | strip
                            endif
                          endif
                        endfor
                        assign dead = false
                        if v.count == 0 and v.active == false
                          assign dead = true
                        endif
                      -%}
                      <label class="alp-opt{% if is_size %} alp-opt--tile{% elsif code != blank %} alp-opt--code{% else %} alp-opt--box{% endif %}{% if dead %} is-dead{% endif %}">
                        <input
                          type="checkbox"
                          name="{{ v.param_name }}"
                          value="{{ v.value }}"
                          {% if v.active %}checked{% endif %}
                          {% if dead %}disabled{% endif %}
                        >
                        {%- if is_size -%}
                          <span class="alp-opt__face">{{ v.label | escape }}</span>
                        {%- elsif code != blank -%}
                          <span class="alp-opt__code">{{ code | escape }}</span><span class="alp-opt__text">{{ v.label | escape }}</span>
                        {%- else -%}
                          <span class="alp-opt__box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="alp-opt__text">{{ v.label | escape }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </label>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </div>
              {%- endcase -%}
            </details>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        <div class="alp-filters__actions">
          <button class="alp-btn" type="submit" data-alp-filter-submit>Show {{ count }} {% if count == 1 %}result{% else %}results{% endif %}</button>
          <button class="alp-btn alp-btn--line alp-d" type="button" data-alp-close>Cancel</button>
          <a class="alp-btn alp-btn--line alp-m" href="{{ collection.url }}?sort_by={{ sort_by | url_encode }}">Clear</a>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  </div>

  {%- if coming_soon -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      An empty collection is a category that hasn't landed: its page is the
      Notify me. Signups are tagged next-drop plus the collection's handle,
      so Admin → Customers can find everyone waiting for it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign soon_tags = 'next-drop, ' | append: collection.handle -%}
    {%- assign soon_img = collection.featured_image | default: section.settings.lifestyle -%}
    <div class="alp-soon">
      <div class="alp-soon__text">
        <span class="alp-badge alp-badge--flare">Next drop</span>
        <h2 class="alp-soon__title">{{ collection.title | escape }}</h2>
        <div class="alp-soon__body">
          {%- if collection.description != blank -%}{{ collection.description }}{%- else -%}<p>{{ section.settings.soon_line | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- render 'alp-signup', id: 'ComingSoon', tags: soon_tags, label: 'Notify me', thanks: "Noted. You'll hear when they land." -%}
        <a class="alp-soon__back" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Shop what's here now</a>
      </div>
      <div class="alp-soon__photo">
        {%- if soon_img != blank -%}
          {{ soon_img | image_url: width: 1600 | image_tag: class: 'alp-fill', loading: 'eager', widths: '800, 1200, 1600', sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw', alt: '' }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
  <div class="alp-cat__tiles">
    {%- liquid
      comment
        Type headings (Shorts, …) only where a page really mixes Types: two
        or more of them, nothing filtered or sorted, and not already on one
        Type's page. Otherwise the photo tiles above say where you are.
      endcomment
      assign types_here = 0
      for t in collection.all_types
        if t == blank
          continue
        endif
        assign in_type = collection.products | where: 'type', t
        if in_type.size > 0
          assign types_here = types_here | plus: 1
        endif
      endfor
      assign grouped = false
      if section.settings.group_by_type and active == 0 and collection.current_type == blank and collection.sort_by == blank and types_here > 1
        assign grouped = true
      endif
      assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 750px) 25vw, 50vw'
      assign i = 0
    -%}
    {%- if grouped -%}
      {%- for t in collection.all_types -%}
        {%- if t == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign in_type = collection.products | where: 'type', t -%}
        {%- if in_type.size == 0 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
        <h2 class="alp-cat__group">
          <span>{{ t | escape }}</span>
          <a href="{{ t | url_for_type }}">See all</a>
        </h2>
        {%- for product in in_type -%}
          {%- assign i = i | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- if i <= 4 -%}{%- assign ld = 'eager' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign ld = 'lazy' -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- render 'alp-card', product: product, loading: ld, look: 'bare', dots: true, sizes: card_sizes -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- capture untyped -%}
        {%- for product in collection.products -%}
          {%- if product.type == blank -%}x{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if untyped != blank -%}
        <h2 class="alp-cat__group"><span>More</span></h2>
        {%- for product in collection.products -%}
          {%- if product.type != blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- render 'alp-card', product: product, loading: 'lazy', look: 'bare', dots: true, sizes: card_sizes -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {{ story }}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- for product in collection.products -%}
        {%- if forloop.index <= 4 -%}{%- assign ld = 'eager' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign ld = 'lazy' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- render 'alp-card', product: product, loading: ld, look: 'bare', dots: true, sizes: card_sizes, video: forloop.first -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The story: after the eighth product (row two of four across, row
          four of two across), or after the last one when there are fewer.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign story_here = false -%}
        {%- if forloop.index == 8 -%}
          {%- assign story_here = true -%}
        {%- elsif forloop.last and forloop.index < 8 -%}
          {%- assign story_here = true -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if story_here -%}{{ story }}{%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <p class="alp-cat__empty">Nothing here yet. {% if active > 0 %}<a href="{{ collection.url }}">Clear the filters</a>{% else %}<a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">See everything</a>{% endif %}</p>
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if paginate.pages > 1 -%}
    <nav class="alp-pages" aria-label="Pages">
      {%- if paginate.previous -%}<a href="{{ paginate.previous.url }}">← Previous</a>{%- endif -%}
      <span>Page {{ paginate.current_page }} of {{ paginate.pages }}</span>
      {%- if paginate.next -%}<a href="{{ paginate.next.url }}">Next →</a>{%- endif -%}
    </nav>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>
{%- endpaginate -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection",
  "tag": "div",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "all_image", "label": "View all photo", "info": "The photo on the View all tile at the top of every collection page. Empty: a product photo is used." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "lifestyle", "label": "Coming-soon photo", "info": "Shown on an empty (coming-soon) collection's page when the collection has no image of its own." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "group_by_type", "label": "Group products by Type", "default": true, "info": "Headings per product Type (Shorts, …) where a page shows two or more Types. Off while a filter or sort is applied." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "soon_line", "label": "Coming-soon line", "default": "Coming in the next drop. Leave your email and we'll let you know the day they land.", "info": "Shown on an empty collection's page, above Notify me. A collection's own description replaces it." },
    {
      "type": "textarea", "id": "codes", "label": "Filter codes",
      "default": "Ultra-lightweight nylon shell: LW\nMoisture-wicking lining: MW\nRear zip pocket: ZP",
      "info": "One per line, \"Filter value: CODE\". Shown as the two-letter code tile in Filters."
    },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Filter buttons show whenever Shopify has filters for the collection (Search & Discovery). Sort by appears once a collection reaches the count set in Theme settings → Bush Riding." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "intro",
      "name": "Story",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "A large photo and a few sentences, shown in the product grid after the second row (the fourth on phones), or after the products while there are only a few." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "match", "label": "Product type or collection handle", "info": "Exactly as in Shopify, e.g. Shorts (a product Type) or bush-riding-launch (a collection's handle). Capitals don't matter." },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photo", "info": "Leave empty for words only." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Small label", "info": "Set small above the headline. Defaults to the type or collection name." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "tagline", "label": "Headline", "info": "e.g. Made for the long way round." },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Text", "info": "Two or three sentences." }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
